Update the existing structured summary with new information. RULES:
- [Preserve established goals, predicates, scope boundaries, relationship filters, temporal conditions, target sets, required mutations, and completion mode unless new messages explicitly change them. Never replace a restricted set with all records or all pending results.]
- [Preserve exact actionable state from the previous summary and new messages, including usable tokens, credentials, variables, API signatures, documentation status, and observed values. Do not reduce it to generic existence claims.]
- [Update the Progress section using only observed completion. Move an item from "In Progress" to "Done" only when the new messages establish completion; do not reopen completed work.]
- [For paginated results, preserve pages retrieved, whether all pages were considered, and every qualifying target. Never treat a full page as proof that pagination is complete.]
- [Keep unresolved facts unresolved. Do not convert uncertainty into a blocker, prohibition, mandatory extraction, alternate-source search, login, verification, deduplication, ordering, duration calculation, or post-action check unless explicitly established.]
- [Preserve the distinction between external actions and informational answers. If the task is action-only, retain an answerless completion requirement; do not invent an answer value.]
- [Preserve exact file paths, function names, error messages, target identifiers, and answer values. Do not alter observed facts or promote an inference to a fact.]

Use this EXACT format:

## Goal
[Preserve existing goals and add only goals explicitly introduced by the new messages. Preserve every task predicate and scope condition exactly.]

## Constraints & Preferences
- [Preserve existing constraints and add only explicit new constraints. Do not add speculative filters, verification, ordering, deduplication, privacy, duration, authentication, or source requirements.]
- [Preserve whether completion requires an answer; do not add an answer requirement to an action-only task.]

## Progress
### Done
- [x] [Include previously established completed items and newly completed items. Preserve complete target sets and pagination status.]
- [x] [Retain exact usable credentials, tokens, variables, API signatures, and documentation already obtained.]

### In Progress
- [ ] [List current work only; do not move unresolved possibilities into mandatory work, and do not reopen completed work.]

### Blocked
- [Current blockers established by the history; remove resolved blockers. Do not call an item blocked merely because an answer is uncertain or an optional route was not found.]

## Key Decisions
- **[Decision]**: [Preserve prior supported decisions and add new supported decisions. Mark inferences as tentative and never assert unsupported dates, relationships, identity matches, sources, capabilities, or completion states.]
- **[Completion mode]**: [Preserve whether the final completion call takes an answer. For action-only tasks, preserve an answerless completion.]

## Next Steps
1. [Update the ordered plan from the established current state. Do not repeat completed documentation, authentication, discovery, or retrieval, and do not add speculative verification, duplicate checks, alternate-source searches, ordering, or post-action work.]
2. [Continue paginated retrieval only as needed to establish all relevant pages, and include every qualifying target already established.]
3. [Use an answer argument only when the task requests information; otherwise complete without one.]

## Critical Context
- [Preserve prior critical context and add new action-critical facts: exact paths, function names, errors, tokens, credentials, variables, dates, target identifiers, observed values, and answer values. Never replace usable context with a generic statement or alter a fact.]
- [Keep established facts, unresolved questions, and unsupported possibilities visibly separate. Do not turn an unresolved possibility into a requirement or blocker.]
- [Remove information only when the new messages explicitly establish that it is obsolete and its removal cannot change the continuation.]

Keep each section concise while preserving all action-critical state, exact identifiers, and completion requirements.
